# p_a3f7 — Standard WFH couple; Marco runs at dawn, shared dinner and TV

Two residents work from home at their separate desks (Marco in the bedroom, Omar in the office) from 9:00 to 17:30 on weekdays. Marco runs 6:30–7:15 before work, taking his running shoes and water bottle out. Both stay home for lunch (12:30–13:15, quick meal at the kitchen table). They cook together 17:30–18:15 and eat at the dining table 18:15–19:00. Evening TV 20:00–22:00 on the couch. Bedtime 23:00. Weekends: sleep in until 9:30, breakfast 10:00, errands 12:00–14:00 (both out with keys and wallets), lunch 14:30, TV 20:00–22:00. What sets this apart: running_shoes_marco and water_bottle_marco are OUT_OF_HOUSE 6:30–7:15 weekdays; the entry hook is bare of jacket_omar at 07:00 (Omar hasn't dressed yet). Refuted if: running shoes are sighted in the house at 06:45 on a weekday, or if both residents are seen in the living room at 06:45.

