# p_d4e9 — Both leave for lunch; the entry is bare at midday

Both residents leave the house together for lunch 12:30–13:30 on weekdays. Keys, wallets, sunglasses, jackets, and shoes all go out. The entry hook and entry table are bare during this window. Dinner at 18:30. Shared TV 20:00–21:30. Weekends: sleep in until 10:30, errands 13:00–15:00 (both out), lunch 15:30, TV 20:00–22:00. What sets this apart: at 13:00 on a weekday, the entry_hook_e1 has NO jackets and the entry_table_e1 has NO keys or wallets. This is the most "travel-heavy" weekday hypothesis. Refuted if: keys_marco or keys_omar are sighted at entry_table_e1 at 13:00 on a weekday, or if both residents are in the house at 12:45 on a weekday.

