# p_7a3e — Standard dual-WFH; Marco's laptop is in his hands during work (fork of p_a1b2)

Marco and Omar both work from home, at their respective desks from roughly 9:00 to 17:30 on weekdays. Neither leaves the house during the workday: keys, wallets, jackets, and running shoes all stay at the entry or shoe rack throughout. The key revision from the parent document is that Marco does not leave his laptop on the desk surface while he works. The robot's 19 empty looks at desk_b1 during 9–17 h (versus only 4 finds) show the laptop is in his hands or on his lap for the bulk of the workday. The charger travels with it. The notebook and pen, by contrast, remain on the desk surface (the pen block held at 0.95 confidence). Nothing in the house leaves: this is a fully contained household.

What sets this fork apart from p_a1b2: the laptop_marco and charger_marco blocks now say ON_PERSON during active work hours rather than desk_b1. The keys and blanket claims are unchanged.

What would refute it: if the robot finds laptop_marco sitting on desk_b1 during a 10–16 h look on a weekday, or finds it in the bedroom or living room rather than ON_PERSON, the ON_PERSON block is wrong. If keys or jackets are ever sighted out of the house, the "nothing leaves" claim collapses.

